<title>USA: Carlyle Inds Q1 continuing shr increases.</title>
<headline>Carlyle Inds Q1 continuing shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>CARLSTADT, N.J. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended March 31,</p>
<p>						     1997     1996</p>
<p> Net sales				     $5,005   $4,871</p>
<p> Income from continuing operations	  851	414</p>
<p> Less dividends on preferred stock	  348	332</p>
<p>Income applicable to common stock</p>
<p>  from continuing operations		  503	 82</p>
<p>Results of discontinued operations net</p>
<p>of income tax provision:</p>
<p>   Income (loss) from operations	  (316)	429</p>
<p>   Loss on disposition		    (9,801)	 --</p>
<p> Total					 (10,117)	429</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			 ( 9,614)	511</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p>     Continuing operations		    .07	.01</p>
<p>     Discontinued operations	     (1.37)	.06</p>
<p> Total					   (1.30)	.07</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding				   7,388    7,399</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Carlyle Industries Inc said its revenues for the first quarter of 1997 exclude the Home Furnishing Division, sold in July 1996 and the Thread Division which was sold in March 1997. The company also said that the 1996 results have been restated in order to account for the two divisions as discontinued operations.</p>
<p>Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
